WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- So, wait, I didn't know this,

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.731
but you started out as a music teacher.

00:00:02.731 --> 00:00:03.564
- I did.

00:00:03.564 --> 00:00:05.090
- I had no clue. Was it elementary?

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:05.923
Is that what it was?

00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:06.870
- Kindergarten through sixth

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.900
in the St. Louis Public School System.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.090
- Wow.
- Yes.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.480
- So, was this so you could...

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.230
I imagine 'cause it's a day job,

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.700
then on the weekends, you gigged?

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.533
- I did.

00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:17.530
I was in a cover band

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.670
and then I got in a
band as a backup singer.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.600
And then I started getting commercials.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.070
A guy walked in who was a producer

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.200
and hired me to sing on
a McDonald's commercial,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.150
which paid me twice what I'd
made in two years of teaching.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.092
- Which is such a statement for teachers.

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:33.758
- Wah wah.
- I know it is. It is.

00:00:33.758 --> 00:00:35.190
It's like sometimes I look at paychecks

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.290
and I'm like, gosh, my mom
works so hard. (laughs)

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.943
- Yes. Yes.
- Yeah.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.490
- And then I started
getting more commercial work

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.610
and I went to LA

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.765
and thought, well I'll get a
record deal and become famous.

00:00:48.765 --> 00:00:49.598
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:50.860
- Like so many. Like in your head.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.940
It happened though, thank you.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.023
'Cause it worked out for us,
too, that got to learn from it.

00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:55.515
- It was all overnight, too.

00:00:55.515 --> 00:00:57.350
- It was? I hate when they do that.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.016
- I know.
- Even for me, I'm like,

00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:00.800
you don't think I worked
before I was on there.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.500
I was like, but okay. Sure.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.195
And even if it was, it's
the longevity that counts.

00:01:04.195 --> 00:01:05.028
- Yeah.

